window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b374-82e91f42f49307a9.json"]={sha256:"82e91f42f49307a9ca814409f9f0dfc451cc559bf1b98acb9b2b73a783b74177",value:{"id":"b374","title":"計軸器列車占用偵測","titleEn":"Axle-counter train-occupancy detection","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦計軸事件守恆方向與資料有效性。從區段軸數守恆建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把輪感測訊號品質與未知占用狀態保存連成可驗證的介面，最後以漏計試驗統計界限整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies axle-count event conservation direction and data validity. Start with axle conservation within a section to define physical or information boundaries, connect wheel-sensor signal quality with preserving unknown occupancy states as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through statistical bounds for missed counts. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-control","subcategoryTitle":"號誌與營運控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Signalling and operational control","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-control","learningTags":["rail","rail-control","control"],"architectureFamily":"rail-control","architectureNodes":[["輪對通過","Wheelset passage"],["感測線圈","Sensing coil"],["事件配對","Event pairing"],["進出計數","Entry exit count"],["有效性狀態","Validity state"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-control","labels":["輪對通過","感測線圈","事件配對","進出計數","有效性狀態"],"labelsEn":["Wheelset passage","Sensing coil","Event pairing","Entry exit count","Validity state"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究區段軸數守恆。原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。公式 y=enter-leave，代入得 y=4 axles。邊界：離線整數守恆模型，不含任何現場重置或解鎖程序。敏感度只改 enter=48 至 49 axles，輸出變為 5 axles；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究雙感測點方向判別：原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。公式 y=spacing/dt，代入得 y=20 m/s。邊界：同一輪對等速通過且事件配對正確，忽略感測區域寬度。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。本單元用標記輪對雙向進出模型區段，核對流入流出與實際區內存量而不連接現場設備。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate axle conservation within a section. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles. Formula y=enter-leave gives y=4 axles. Boundary: Offline integer-conservation model without any real reset or release procedure. For sensitivity, change only enter=48 to 49 axles; the output becomes 5 axles. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate direction from paired sensing points: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s. Formula y=spacing/dt gives y=20 m/s. Boundary: One wheelset moving at constant speed with correct event pairing; sensing-zone width is neglected. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Move marked model wheelsets through a section in both directions and compare entry, exit and actual occupancy without connecting to field equipment. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b374-v16-s1","title":"區段軸數守恆與雙感測點方向判別","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section & Direction from paired sensing points","description":"本階段聚焦「區段軸數守恆」與「雙感測點方向判別」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Axle conservation within a section\" and \"Direction from paired sensing points\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b374-v16-01","title":"區段軸數守恆：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「區段軸數守恆」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Axle conservation within a section” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元用標記輪對雙向進出模型區段，核對流入流出與實際區內存量而不連接現場設備。計軸占用利用邊界流入與流出守恆，計數差不是列車位置量測。差值為零仍需邊界感測器、方向判斷與狀態可信度成立；未知或故障狀態不能僅因兩個數字相等就自動宣告清空。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：離線整數守恆模型，不含任何現場重置或解鎖程序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「區段軸數守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Move marked model wheelsets through a section in both directions and compare entry, exit and actual occupancy without connecting to field equipment. Axle counting applies conservation at section boundaries; the count difference is not a position measurement. A zero difference is useful only when boundary sensing, direction and state validity are trustworthy. Unknown or failed states cannot be declared clear merely because two numbers match. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Offline integer-conservation model without any real reset or release procedure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Axle conservation within a section” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles.","failure":"常見誤解：「進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「區段軸數守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Axle conservation within a section”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-01-k1","title":"區段軸數守恆","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section","text":"本單元用標記輪對雙向進出模型區段，核對流入流出與實際區內存量而不連接現場設備。計軸占用利用邊界流入與流出守恆，計數差不是列車位置量測。","textEn":"Move marked model wheelsets through a section in both directions and compare entry, exit and actual occupancy without connecting to field equipment. Axle counting applies conservation at section boundaries; the count difference is not a position measurement.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「區段軸數守恆」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Axle conservation within a section\" is correct?","options":["進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車","本單元用標記輪對雙向進出模型區段，核對流入流出與實際區內存量而不連接現場設備。","感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度"],"optionsEn":["Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty.","Move marked model wheelsets through a section in both directions and compare entry, exit and actual occupancy without connecting to field equipment.","Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元用標記輪對雙向進出模型區段，核對流入流出與實際區內存量而不連接現場設備。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Move marked model wheelsets through a section in both directions and compare entry, exit and actual occupancy without connecting to field equipment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b374-v16-02","title":"區段軸數守恆：定量估算","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「區段軸數守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Axle conservation within a section” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。公式 y=enter-leave，代入得 y=4 axles。邊界：離線整數守恆模型，不含任何現場重置或解鎖程序。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles. Formula y=enter-leave gives y=4 axles. Boundary: Offline integer-conservation model without any real reset or release procedure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以標記輪對的玩具車雙向重播，對照人工真值、事件順序與感測器有效旗標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay a marked model vehicle in both directions and compare manual truth, event ordering and sensor-validity flags.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。公式 y=enter-leave，代入得 y=4 axles。邊界：離線整數守恆模型，不含任何現場重置或解鎖程序。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles. Formula y=enter-leave gives y=4 axles. Boundary: Offline integer-conservation model without any real reset or release procedure.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「區段軸數守恆」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Axle conservation within a section\", which statement holds?","options":["總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好","只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。"],"optionsEn":["A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.","The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：進入軸數 enter=48 axles；離開軸數 leave=44 axles。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: entering axles enter=48 axles; leaving axles leave=44 axles. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b374-v16-03","title":"區段軸數守恆：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「區段軸數守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Axle conservation within a section” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以標記輪對的玩具車雙向重播，對照人工真值、事件順序與感測器有效旗標。以「區段軸數守恆」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay a marked model vehicle in both directions and compare manual truth, event ordering and sensor-validity flags. For axle conservation within a section, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把進入軸數 enter 從 48 改成 49 axles（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 4 變為 5 axles。先說明「區段軸數守恆」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only entering axles enter from 48 to 49 axles (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 4 to 5 axles. Explain the causal direction for axle conservation within a section, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：漏計與多計可能互相抵消形成假零值，方向錯誤則會讓計數增減的符號顛倒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Missed and extra counts can cancel into a false zero, while direction errors reverse the signs of increments. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以標記輪對的玩具車雙向重播，對照人工真值、事件順序與感測器有效旗標。以「區段軸數守恆」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Replay a marked model vehicle in both directions and compare manual truth, event ordering and sensor-validity flags. For axle conservation within a section, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把進入軸數 enter 從 48 改成 49 axles（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 4 變為 5 axles。先說明「區段軸數守恆」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only entering axles enter from 48 to 49 axles (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 4 to 5 axles. Explain the causal direction for axle conservation within a section, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「區段軸數守恆」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Axle conservation within a section\"?","options":["以標記輪對的玩具車雙向重播，對照人工真值、事件順序與感測器有效旗標。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Replay a marked model vehicle in both directions and compare manual truth, event ordering and sensor-validity flags.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以標記輪對的玩具車雙向重播，對照人工真值、事件順序與感測器有效旗標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay a marked model vehicle in both directions and compare manual truth, event ordering and sensor-validity flags. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b374-v16-04","title":"區段軸數守恆：失效診斷","titleEn":"Axle conservation within a section: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「區段軸數守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Axle conservation within a section” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏計與多計可能互相抵消形成假零值，方向錯誤則會讓計數增減的符號顛倒。回到「區段軸數守恆」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Missed and extra counts can cancel into a false zero, while direction errors reverse the signs of increments. Trace the input chain for axle conservation within a section. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：離線整數守恆模型，不含任何現場重置或解鎖程序。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Offline integer-conservation model without any real reset or release procedure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏計與多計可能互相抵消形成假零值，方向錯誤則會讓計數增減的符號顛倒。回到「區段軸數守恆」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Missed and extra counts can cancel into a false zero, while direction errors reverse the signs of increments. Trace the input chain for axle conservation within a section. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「區段軸數守恆」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Axle conservation within a section\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","漏計與多計可能互相抵消形成假零值，方向錯誤則會讓計數增減的符號顛倒。","感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Missed and extra counts can cancel into a false zero, while direction errors reverse the signs of increments.","Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏計與多計可能互相抵消形成假零值，方向錯誤則會讓計數增減的符號顛倒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Missed and extra counts can cancel into a false zero, while direction errors reverse the signs of increments. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b374-v16-05","title":"雙感測點方向判別：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Direction from paired sensing points: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「雙感測點方向判別」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Direction from paired sensing points” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元利用同一輪對通過兩個感測點的先後順序，特別檢查低速回滾時的事件配對。兩個相鄰感測點的事件先後順序可提供方向，間距除以時間差可估局部速度。時間解析度與輪緣幾何都影響結果；接近停車或往返擺動時，事件配對比公式本身更容易出錯。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：同一輪對等速通過且事件配對正確，忽略感測區域寬度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙感測點方向判別」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use the order in which one wheelset passes two sensing points, paying particular attention to event pairing during slow rollback. Event ordering across two nearby sensors provides direction, while separation divided by transit time estimates local speed. Timing resolution and wheel geometry affect the estimate. Near standstill or during oscillatory movement, pairing the correct events is often harder than evaluating the equation. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: One wheelset moving at constant speed with correct event pairing; sensing-zone width is neglected. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Direction from paired sensing points” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙感測點方向判別」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Direction from paired sensing points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-05-k1","title":"雙感測點方向判別","titleEn":"Direction from paired sensing points","text":"本單元利用同一輪對通過兩個感測點的先後順序，特別檢查低速回滾時的事件配對。兩個相鄰感測點的事件先後順序可提供方向，間距除以時間差可估局部速度。","textEn":"Use the order in which one wheelset passes two sensing points, paying particular attention to event pairing during slow rollback. Event ordering across two nearby sensors provides direction, while separation divided by transit time estimates local speed.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙感測點方向判別」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Direction from paired sensing points\" is correct?","options":["感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度","取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同","本單元利用同一輪對通過兩個感測點的先後順序，特別檢查低速回滾時的事件配對。"],"optionsEn":["Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed.","Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.","Use the order in which one wheelset passes two sensing points, paying particular attention to event pairing during slow rollback."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元利用同一輪對通過兩個感測點的先後順序，特別檢查低速回滾時的事件配對。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use the order in which one wheelset passes two sensing points, paying particular attention to event pairing during slow rollback. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b374-v16-06","title":"雙感測點方向判別：定量估算","titleEn":"Direction from paired sensing points: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙感測點方向判別」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Direction from paired sensing points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。公式 y=spacing/dt，代入得 y=20 m/s。邊界：同一輪對等速通過且事件配對正確，忽略感測區域寬度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s. Formula y=spacing/dt gives y=20 m/s. Boundary: One wheelset moving at constant speed with correct event pairing; sensing-zone width is neglected. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用獨立位置尺與時間基準核對事件配對，包含低速、停止與反向的離線測試。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check event pairing against an independent ruler and clock, including low-speed, stopped and reversed offline tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。公式 y=spacing/dt，代入得 y=20 m/s。邊界：同一輪對等速通過且事件配對正確，忽略感測區域寬度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s. Formula y=spacing/dt gives y=20 m/s. Boundary: One wheelset moving at constant speed with correct event pairing; sensing-zone width is neglected.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙感測點方向判別」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Direction from paired sensing points\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：感測點間距 spacing=0.3 m；通過時間差 dt=0.015 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensor separation spacing=0.3 m; passage time difference dt=0.015 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b374-v16-07","title":"雙感測點方向判別：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Direction from paired sensing points: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙感測點方向判別」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Direction from paired sensing points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用獨立位置尺與時間基準核對事件配對，包含低速、停止與反向的離線測試。以「雙感測點方向判別」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check event pairing against an independent ruler and clock, including low-speed, stopped and reversed offline tests. For direction from paired sensing points, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把通過時間差 dt 從 0.015 改成 0.0165 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 20 變為 18.1818 m/s。先說明「雙感測點方向判別」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only passage time difference dt from 0.015 to 0.0165 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 20 to 18.1818 m/s. Explain the causal direction for direction from paired sensing points, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：將不同輪對的脈衝配成一對會產生不合理速度，反向回滾也會破壞單純遞增事件假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pairing pulses from different wheelsets produces implausible speed; rollback violates assumptions of monotonically ordered events. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用獨立位置尺與時間基準核對事件配對，包含低速、停止與反向的離線測試。以「雙感測點方向判別」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Check event pairing against an independent ruler and clock, including low-speed, stopped and reversed offline tests. For direction from paired sensing points, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把通過時間差 dt 從 0.015 改成 0.0165 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 20 變為 18.1818 m/s。先說明「雙感測點方向判別」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only passage time difference dt from 0.015 to 0.0165 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 20 to 18.1818 m/s. Explain the causal direction for direction from paired sensing points, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙感測點方向判別」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Direction from paired sensing points\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","使用獨立位置尺與時間基準核對事件配對，包含低速、停止與反向的離線測試。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Check event pairing against an independent ruler and clock, including low-speed, stopped and reversed offline tests.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用獨立位置尺與時間基準核對事件配對，包含低速、停止與反向的離線測試。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check event pairing against an independent ruler and clock, including low-speed, stopped and reversed offline tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b374-v16-08","title":"雙感測點方向判別：失效診斷","titleEn":"Direction from paired sensing points: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙感測點方向判別」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Direction from paired sensing points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將不同輪對的脈衝配成一對會產生不合理速度，反向回滾也會破壞單純遞增事件假設。回到「雙感測點方向判別」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pairing pulses from different wheelsets produces implausible speed; rollback violates assumptions of monotonically ordered events. Trace the input chain for direction from paired sensing points. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：同一輪對等速通過且事件配對正確，忽略感測區域寬度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: One wheelset moving at constant speed with correct event pairing; sensing-zone width is neglected.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將不同輪對的脈衝配成一對會產生不合理速度，反向回滾也會破壞單純遞增事件假設。回到「雙感測點方向判別」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Pairing pulses from different wheelsets produces implausible speed; rollback violates assumptions of monotonically ordered events. Trace the input chain for direction from paired sensing points. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙感測點方向判別」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Direction from paired sensing points\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同","將不同輪對的脈衝配成一對會產生不合理速度，反向回滾也會破壞單純遞增事件假設。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.","Pairing pulses from different wheelsets produces implausible speed; rollback violates assumptions of monotonically ordered events."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將不同輪對的脈衝配成一對會產生不合理速度，反向回滾也會破壞單純遞增事件假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pairing pulses from different wheelsets produces implausible speed; rollback violates assumptions of monotonically ordered events. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b374-v16-s2","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度與輪感測訊號品質","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses & Wheel-sensor signal quality","description":"本階段聚焦「輪脈衝時間解析度」與「輪感測訊號品質」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses\" and \"Wheel-sensor signal quality\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b374-v16-09","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「輪脈衝時間解析度」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元比較不同通過速度的脈衝寬度與取樣間隔，判斷資料列數是否足以保留事件邊界。固定時間取樣在移動系統中對應空間間隔，速度越高相同頻率越容易漏過狹窄特徵。時間戳抖動會讓空間取樣不均勻；提高取樣率仍需足夠感測頻寬與抗混疊處理，不能只增加資料列數。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：等速與等時間取樣的間距，不代表可以解析同樣大小的最小缺陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輪脈衝時間解析度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare pulse width and sampling interval at different passage speeds, assessing whether the samples preserve the event boundaries. Time sampling in a moving system corresponds to spatial spacing; at higher speed, the same rate can miss narrow features. Timestamp jitter makes spatial samples nonuniform. A higher rate still requires adequate sensor bandwidth and anti-alias filtering, rather than merely more rows of data. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Spacing for constant speed and uniform sampling; it is not automatically the smallest resolvable defect size. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：移動速度 v=25 m/s；取樣頻率 f=20 Hz。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: motion speed v=25 m/s; sampling frequency f=20 Hz.","failure":"常見誤解：「取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輪脈衝時間解析度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-09-k1","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses","text":"本單元比較不同通過速度的脈衝寬度與取樣間隔，判斷資料列數是否足以保留事件邊界。固定時間取樣在移動系統中對應空間間隔，速度越高相同頻率越容易漏過狹窄特徵。","textEn":"Compare pulse width and sampling interval at different passage speeds, assessing whether the samples preserve the event boundaries. Time sampling in a moving system corresponds to spatial spacing; at higher speed, the same rate can miss narrow features.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輪脈衝時間解析度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses\" is correct?","options":["本單元比較不同通過速度的脈衝寬度與取樣間隔，判斷資料列數是否足以保留事件邊界。","取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Compare pulse width and sampling interval at different passage speeds, assessing whether the samples preserve the event boundaries.","Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元比較不同通過速度的脈衝寬度與取樣間隔，判斷資料列數是否足以保留事件邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare pulse width and sampling interval at different passage speeds, assessing whether the samples preserve the event boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b374-v16-10","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度：定量估算","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輪脈衝時間解析度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：移動速度 v=25 m/s；取樣頻率 f=20 Hz。公式 y=v/f，代入得 y=1.25 m/sample。邊界：等速與等時間取樣的間距，不代表可以解析同樣大小的最小缺陷。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: motion speed v=25 m/s; sampling frequency f=20 Hz. Formula y=v/f gives y=1.25 m/sample. Boundary: Spacing for constant speed and uniform sampling; it is not automatically the smallest resolvable defect size. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對已知長度特徵以不同速度重播，檢查事件是否保留並比較位置內插誤差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay a known-length feature at different speeds, check event retention, and compare position-interpolation error.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：移動速度 v=25 m/s；取樣頻率 f=20 Hz。公式 y=v/f，代入得 y=1.25 m/sample。邊界：等速與等時間取樣的間距，不代表可以解析同樣大小的最小缺陷。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: motion speed v=25 m/s; sampling frequency f=20 Hz. Formula y=v/f gives y=1.25 m/sample. Boundary: Spacing for constant speed and uniform sampling; it is not automatically the smallest resolvable defect size.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輪脈衝時間解析度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses\", which statement holds?","options":["只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","原創假想教學輸入：移動速度 v=25 m/s；取樣頻率 f=20 Hz。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: motion speed v=25 m/s; sampling frequency f=20 Hz.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：移動速度 v=25 m/s；取樣頻率 f=20 Hz。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: motion speed v=25 m/s; sampling frequency f=20 Hz. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b374-v16-11","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輪脈衝時間解析度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對已知長度特徵以不同速度重播，檢查事件是否保留並比較位置內插誤差。以「輪脈衝時間解析度」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay a known-length feature at different speeds, check event retention, and compare position-interpolation error. For temporal resolution of wheel pulses, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把移動速度 v 從 25 改成 27.5 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.25 變為 1.375 m/sample。先說明「輪脈衝時間解析度」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only motion speed v from 25 to 27.5 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.25 to 1.375 m/sample. Explain the causal direction for temporal resolution of wheel pulses, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：高頻振動混疊成低頻漂移可能被誤判為幾何偏差，遺失時間戳也會破壞空間重建。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High-frequency vibration can alias into apparent low-frequency geometry drift; missing timestamps also corrupt spatial reconstruction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對已知長度特徵以不同速度重播，檢查事件是否保留並比較位置內插誤差。以「輪脈衝時間解析度」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Replay a known-length feature at different speeds, check event retention, and compare position-interpolation error. For temporal resolution of wheel pulses, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把移動速度 v 從 25 改成 27.5 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.25 變為 1.375 m/sample。先說明「輪脈衝時間解析度」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only motion speed v from 25 to 27.5 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.25 to 1.375 m/sample. Explain the causal direction for temporal resolution of wheel pulses, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輪脈衝時間解析度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","對已知長度特徵以不同速度重播，檢查事件是否保留並比較位置內插誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","Replay a known-length feature at different speeds, check event retention, and compare position-interpolation error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對已知長度特徵以不同速度重播，檢查事件是否保留並比較位置內插誤差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay a known-length feature at different speeds, check event retention, and compare position-interpolation error. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b374-v16-12","title":"輪脈衝時間解析度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輪脈衝時間解析度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Temporal resolution of wheel pulses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高頻振動混疊成低頻漂移可能被誤判為幾何偏差，遺失時間戳也會破壞空間重建。回到「輪脈衝時間解析度」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High-frequency vibration can alias into apparent low-frequency geometry drift; missing timestamps also corrupt spatial reconstruction. Trace the input chain for temporal resolution of wheel pulses. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：等速與等時間取樣的間距，不代表可以解析同樣大小的最小缺陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Spacing for constant speed and uniform sampling; it is not automatically the smallest resolvable defect size.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高頻振動混疊成低頻漂移可能被誤判為幾何偏差，遺失時間戳也會破壞空間重建。回到「輪脈衝時間解析度」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"High-frequency vibration can alias into apparent low-frequency geometry drift; missing timestamps also corrupt spatial reconstruction. Trace the input chain for temporal resolution of wheel pulses. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輪脈衝時間解析度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temporal resolution of wheel pulses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高頻振動混疊成低頻漂移可能被誤判為幾何偏差，遺失時間戳也會破壞空間重建。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["High-frequency vibration can alias into apparent low-frequency geometry drift; missing timestamps also corrupt spatial reconstruction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高頻振動混疊成低頻漂移可能被誤判為幾何偏差，遺失時間戳也會破壞空間重建。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High-frequency vibration can alias into apparent low-frequency geometry drift; missing timestamps also corrupt spatial reconstruction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b374-v16-13","title":"輪感測訊號品質：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wheel-sensor signal quality: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「輪感測訊號品質」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wheel-sensor signal quality” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將金屬輪對訊號與外部干擾分開量測，使用相同頻寬比較訊雜比而不設定現場門檻。以相同阻抗下的電壓比換算訊雜比時使用二十倍對數。訊號與雜訊必須採一致頻寬與有效值定義；只把量測頻寬縮小可能讓數字改善，卻同時刪掉辨識狀態所需的訊息。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輪感測訊號品質」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Measure wheel-related signal and external interference separately, comparing signal quality at equal bandwidth without prescribing field thresholds. Voltage-ratio signal-to-noise uses twenty times the logarithm when impedances match. Signal and noise must share bandwidth and RMS definitions. Narrowing measurement bandwidth can improve the number while removing information needed to distinguish states. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wheel-sensor signal quality” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms.","failure":"常見誤解：「總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輪感測訊號品質」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wheel-sensor signal quality”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-13-k1","title":"輪感測訊號品質","titleEn":"Wheel-sensor signal quality","text":"本單元將金屬輪對訊號與外部干擾分開量測，使用相同頻寬比較訊雜比而不設定現場門檻。以相同阻抗下的電壓比換算訊雜比時使用二十倍對數。","textEn":"Measure wheel-related signal and external interference separately, comparing signal quality at equal bandwidth without prescribing field thresholds. Voltage-ratio signal-to-noise uses twenty times the logarithm when impedances match.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輪感測訊號品質」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wheel-sensor signal quality\" is correct?","options":["總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好","本單元將金屬輪對訊號與外部干擾分開量測，使用相同頻寬比較訊雜比而不設定現場門檻。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.","Measure wheel-related signal and external interference separately, comparing signal quality at equal bandwidth without prescribing field thresholds.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元將金屬輪對訊號與外部干擾分開量測，使用相同頻寬比較訊雜比而不設定現場門檻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Measure wheel-related signal and external interference separately, comparing signal quality at equal bandwidth without prescribing field thresholds. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b374-v16-14","title":"輪感測訊號品質：定量估算","titleEn":"Wheel-sensor signal quality: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輪感測訊號品質」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wheel-sensor signal quality” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。公式 y=20*log10(signal/noise)，代入得 y=26.0206 dB。邊界：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Formula y=20*log10(signal/noise) gives y=26.0206 dB. Boundary: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。公式 y=20*log10(signal/noise)，代入得 y=26.0206 dB。邊界：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Formula y=20*log10(signal/noise) gives y=26.0206 dB. Boundary: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輪感測訊號品質」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wheel-sensor signal quality\", which statement holds?","options":["狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。"],"optionsEn":["Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b374-v16-15","title":"輪感測訊號品質：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wheel-sensor signal quality: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輪感測訊號品質」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wheel-sensor signal quality” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。以「輪感測訊號品質」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. For wheel-sensor signal quality, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把雜訊有效值 noise 從 0.1 改成 0.11 V_rms（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 26.0206 變為 25.1927 dB。先說明「輪感測訊號品質」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only noise RMS noise from 0.1 to 0.11 V_rms (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 26.0206 to 25.1927 dB. Explain the causal direction for wheel-sensor signal quality, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。以「輪感測訊號品質」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. For wheel-sensor signal quality, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把雜訊有效值 noise 從 0.1 改成 0.11 V_rms（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 26.0206 變為 25.1927 dB。先說明「輪感測訊號品質」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only noise RMS noise from 0.1 to 0.11 V_rms (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 26.0206 to 25.1927 dB. Explain the causal direction for wheel-sensor signal quality, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輪感測訊號品質」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wheel-sensor signal quality\"?","options":["將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車"],"optionsEn":["Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b374-v16-16","title":"輪感測訊號品質：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wheel-sensor signal quality: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輪感測訊號品質」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wheel-sensor signal quality” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。回到「輪感測訊號品質」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Trace the input chain for wheel-sensor signal quality. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。回到「輪感測訊號品質」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Trace the input chain for wheel-sensor signal quality. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輪感測訊號品質」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wheel-sensor signal quality\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b374-v16-s3","title":"計軸事件排序與計數訊息遺失分析","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events & Loss of count-event messages","description":"本階段聚焦「計軸事件排序」與「計數訊息遺失分析」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ordering axle-count events\" and \"Loss of count-event messages\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b374-v16-17","title":"計軸事件排序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「計軸事件排序」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ordering axle-count events” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元追蹤分散感測點的時間偏差，檢查資料延後抵達時是否仍能保留原始事件順序。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。多系統事件排序若依不同時鐘，可能把因果順序顛倒；校時跳變又會使量測區間長度失真，所以需記錄時鐘品質與校正事件。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「計軸事件排序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Track clock offsets among distributed sensing points, checking whether original event order survives delayed message arrival. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset. Ordering multisystem events on different clocks can reverse apparent causality. Synchronization jumps can distort interval lengths, so clock quality and correction events must be recorded. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ordering axle-count events” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「計軸事件排序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ordering axle-count events”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-17-k1","title":"計軸事件排序","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events","text":"本單元追蹤分散感測點的時間偏差，檢查資料延後抵達時是否仍能保留原始事件順序。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。","textEn":"Track clock offsets among distributed sensing points, checking whether original event order survives delayed message arrival. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「計軸事件排序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ordering axle-count events\" is correct?","options":["測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","本單元追蹤分散感測點的時間偏差，檢查資料延後抵達時是否仍能保留原始事件順序。"],"optionsEn":["Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Track clock offsets among distributed sensing points, checking whether original event order survives delayed message arrival."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元追蹤分散感測點的時間偏差，檢查資料延後抵達時是否仍能保留原始事件順序。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Track clock offsets among distributed sensing points, checking whether original event order survives delayed message arrival. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b374-v16-18","title":"計軸事件排序：定量估算","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「計軸事件排序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ordering axle-count events” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「計軸事件排序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ordering axle-count events\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b374-v16-19","title":"計軸事件排序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「計軸事件排序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ordering axle-count events” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「計軸事件排序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For ordering axle-count events, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「計軸事件排序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for ordering axle-count events, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「計軸事件排序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For ordering axle-count events, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「計軸事件排序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for ordering axle-count events, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「計軸事件排序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ordering axle-count events\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b374-v16-20","title":"計軸事件排序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ordering axle-count events: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「計軸事件排序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ordering axle-count events” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「計軸事件排序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for ordering axle-count events. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「計軸事件排序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for ordering axle-count events. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「計軸事件排序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ordering axle-count events\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b374-v16-21","title":"計數訊息遺失分析：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Loss of count-event messages: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「計數訊息遺失分析」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Loss of count-event messages” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元區分事件沒有產生與事件產生後傳送遺失，透過源端紀錄和接收端紀錄交叉比對。獨立封包遺失可以相乘得到連續遺失機率，但實際無線遮蔽常造成成串遺失。增加重送次數會占用時間與頻寬，不能把可靠度與時效分開最佳化；舊封包即使最後送達，也可能已不適合當前控制。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：明確假設各次遺失獨立同分布，不適用遮蔽引起的相關失聯。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「計數訊息遺失分析」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish an event that was never generated from one lost after generation by comparing source-side and receiver-side records. Independent packet losses multiply to give a consecutive-loss probability, but radio obstruction often causes correlated bursts. Retransmissions consume time and bandwidth, so reliability and freshness cannot be optimized independently. A packet eventually delivered may already be too old for the current control decision. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Losses are explicitly independent and identically distributed; correlated outages are outside the model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Loss of count-event messages” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立遺失率 p=0.02 1；連續封包數 n=3 packets。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent loss probability p=0.02 1; consecutive packet count n=3 packets.","failure":"常見誤解：「只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「計數訊息遺失分析」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Loss of count-event messages”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-21-k1","title":"計數訊息遺失分析","titleEn":"Loss of count-event messages","text":"本單元區分事件沒有產生與事件產生後傳送遺失，透過源端紀錄和接收端紀錄交叉比對。獨立封包遺失可以相乘得到連續遺失機率，但實際無線遮蔽常造成成串遺失。","textEn":"Distinguish an event that was never generated from one lost after generation by comparing source-side and receiver-side records. Independent packet losses multiply to give a consecutive-loss probability, but radio obstruction often causes correlated bursts.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「計數訊息遺失分析」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Loss of count-event messages\" is correct?","options":["本單元區分事件沒有產生與事件產生後傳送遺失，透過源端紀錄和接收端紀錄交叉比對。","只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Distinguish an event that was never generated from one lost after generation by comparing source-side and receiver-side records.","The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元區分事件沒有產生與事件產生後傳送遺失，透過源端紀錄和接收端紀錄交叉比對。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish an event that was never generated from one lost after generation by comparing source-side and receiver-side records. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b374-v16-22","title":"計數訊息遺失分析：定量估算","titleEn":"Loss of count-event messages: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「計數訊息遺失分析」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Loss of count-event messages” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立遺失率 p=0.02 1；連續封包數 n=3 packets。公式 y=p**n，代入得 y=8e-06 1。邊界：明確假設各次遺失獨立同分布，不適用遮蔽引起的相關失聯。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent loss probability p=0.02 1; consecutive packet count n=3 packets. Formula y=p**n gives y=8e-06 1. Boundary: Losses are explicitly independent and identically distributed; correlated outages are outside the model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時統計單包遺失率與最長連續遺失段，將結果和獨立模型比較以辨識相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure single-packet loss and the longest loss burst together, then compare them with the independent model to identify correlation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立遺失率 p=0.02 1；連續封包數 n=3 packets。公式 y=p**n，代入得 y=8e-06 1。邊界：明確假設各次遺失獨立同分布，不適用遮蔽引起的相關失聯。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent loss probability p=0.02 1; consecutive packet count n=3 packets. Formula y=p**n gives y=8e-06 1. Boundary: Losses are explicitly independent and identically distributed; correlated outages are outside the model.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「計數訊息遺失分析」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Loss of count-event messages\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：獨立遺失率 p=0.02 1；連續封包數 n=3 packets。","進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent loss probability p=0.02 1; consecutive packet count n=3 packets.","Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立遺失率 p=0.02 1；連續封包數 n=3 packets。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent loss probability p=0.02 1; consecutive packet count n=3 packets. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b374-v16-23","title":"計數訊息遺失分析：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Loss of count-event messages: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「計數訊息遺失分析」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Loss of count-event messages” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時統計單包遺失率與最長連續遺失段，將結果和獨立模型比較以辨識相關性。以「計數訊息遺失分析」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure single-packet loss and the longest loss burst together, then compare them with the independent model to identify correlation. For loss of count-event messages, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把獨立遺失率 p 從 0.02 改成 0.022 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8e-06 變為 1.0648e-05 1。先說明「計數訊息遺失分析」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only independent loss probability p from 0.02 to 0.022 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8e-06 to 1.0648e-05 1. Explain the causal direction for loss of count-event messages, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把成串失聯當成獨立事件會嚴重低估尾端風險，時間戳重排也可能讓重送掩蓋陳舊資料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating burst outages as independent events understates tail risk; reordered timestamps may also hide stale retransmissions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時統計單包遺失率與最長連續遺失段，將結果和獨立模型比較以辨識相關性。以「計數訊息遺失分析」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure single-packet loss and the longest loss burst together, then compare them with the independent model to identify correlation. For loss of count-event messages, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把獨立遺失率 p 從 0.02 改成 0.022 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8e-06 變為 1.0648e-05 1。先說明「計數訊息遺失分析」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only independent loss probability p from 0.02 to 0.022 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8e-06 to 1.0648e-05 1. Explain the causal direction for loss of count-event messages, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「計數訊息遺失分析」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Loss of count-event messages\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同","同時統計單包遺失率與最長連續遺失段，將結果和獨立模型比較以辨識相關性。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.","Measure single-packet loss and the longest loss burst together, then compare them with the independent model to identify correlation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同時統計單包遺失率與最長連續遺失段，將結果和獨立模型比較以辨識相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure single-packet loss and the longest loss burst together, then compare them with the independent model to identify correlation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b374-v16-24","title":"計數訊息遺失分析：失效診斷","titleEn":"Loss of count-event messages: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「計數訊息遺失分析」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Loss of count-event messages” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把成串失聯當成獨立事件會嚴重低估尾端風險，時間戳重排也可能讓重送掩蓋陳舊資料。回到「計數訊息遺失分析」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating burst outages as independent events understates tail risk; reordered timestamps may also hide stale retransmissions. Trace the input chain for loss of count-event messages. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：明確假設各次遺失獨立同分布，不適用遮蔽引起的相關失聯。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Losses are explicitly independent and identically distributed; correlated outages are outside the model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把成串失聯當成獨立事件會嚴重低估尾端風險，時間戳重排也可能讓重送掩蓋陳舊資料。回到「計數訊息遺失分析」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Treating burst outages as independent events understates tail risk; reordered timestamps may also hide stale retransmissions. Trace the input chain for loss of count-event messages. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「計數訊息遺失分析」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Loss of count-event messages\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把成串失聯當成獨立事件會嚴重低估尾端風險，時間戳重排也可能讓重送掩蓋陳舊資料。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Treating burst outages as independent events understates tail risk; reordered timestamps may also hide stale retransmissions.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把成串失聯當成獨立事件會嚴重低估尾端風險，時間戳重排也可能讓重送掩蓋陳舊資料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating burst outages as independent events understates tail risk; reordered timestamps may also hide stale retransmissions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b374-v16-s4","title":"未知占用狀態保存與計軸感測共同原因","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states & Common causes in axle sensing","description":"本階段聚焦「未知占用狀態保存」與「計軸感測共同原因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Preserving unknown occupancy states\" and \"Common causes in axle sensing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b374-v16-25","title":"未知占用狀態保存：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「未知占用狀態保存」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Preserving unknown occupancy states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把計數值和有效旗標分開建模，當資料不完整時保留未知而不默認區段清空。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。可達性約束能排除不可能組合，但刪除條件必須有證據；安全性質通常針對所有可達狀態，而非幾個畫面上看起來合理的狀態。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「未知占用狀態保存」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Model count values separately from validity flags, retaining an unknown state when data is incomplete rather than defaulting to a clear section. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective. Reachability constraints can eliminate impossible combinations, but each exclusion needs justification. Safety properties normally concern every reachable state rather than a few states that look plausible on a display. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Preserving unknown occupancy states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","failure":"常見誤解：「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「未知占用狀態保存」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Preserving unknown occupancy states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-25-k1","title":"未知占用狀態保存","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states","text":"本單元把計數值和有效旗標分開建模，當資料不完整時保留未知而不默認區段清空。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。","textEn":"Model count values separately from validity flags, retaining an unknown state when data is incomplete rather than defaulting to a clear section. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「未知占用狀態保存」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Preserving unknown occupancy states\" is correct?","options":["狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","本單元把計數值和有效旗標分開建模，當資料不完整時保留未知而不默認區段清空。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Model count values separately from validity flags, retaining an unknown state when data is incomplete rather than defaulting to a clear section.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元把計數值和有效旗標分開建模，當資料不完整時保留未知而不默認區段清空。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Model count values separately from validity flags, retaining an unknown state when data is incomplete rather than defaulting to a clear section. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b374-v16-26","title":"未知占用狀態保存：定量估算","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「未知占用狀態保存」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Preserving unknown occupancy states” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「未知占用狀態保存」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Preserving unknown occupancy states\", which statement holds?","options":["完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度","原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。"],"optionsEn":["Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b374-v16-27","title":"未知占用狀態保存：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「未知占用狀態保存」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Preserving unknown occupancy states” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「未知占用狀態保存」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For preserving unknown occupancy states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「未知占用狀態保存」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for preserving unknown occupancy states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「未知占用狀態保存」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For preserving unknown occupancy states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「未知占用狀態保存」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for preserving unknown occupancy states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「未知占用狀態保存」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Preserving unknown occupancy states\"?","options":["用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b374-v16-28","title":"未知占用狀態保存：失效診斷","titleEn":"Preserving unknown occupancy states: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「未知占用狀態保存」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Preserving unknown occupancy states” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「未知占用狀態保存」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for preserving unknown occupancy states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「未知占用狀態保存」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for preserving unknown occupancy states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「未知占用狀態保存」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Preserving unknown occupancy states\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b374-v16-29","title":"計軸感測共同原因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Common causes in axle sensing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「計軸感測共同原因」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Common causes in axle sensing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元檢查兩個感測通道是否受同一安裝位移或電磁環境影響，避免把相關輸入當獨立證據。兩支路都失效才失去功能的架構可降低獨立故障貢獻，卻不能消除共同原因。共同電源、相同軟體缺陷或同處淹水會同時影響兩支路；因此增加硬體數量不能取代分離、異質性與失效偵測的證據。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「計軸感測共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Examine whether two sensing channels share installation movement or electromagnetic exposure, avoiding treatment of correlated inputs as independent evidence. A function lost only when both branches fail can reduce independent contributions but cannot eliminate common causes. Shared power, identical software defects or flooding at one location can affect both branches. More hardware does not replace evidence for separation, diversity and fault detection. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Common causes in axle sensing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「計軸感測共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Common causes in axle sensing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-29-k1","title":"計軸感測共同原因","titleEn":"Common causes in axle sensing","text":"本單元檢查兩個感測通道是否受同一安裝位移或電磁環境影響，避免把相關輸入當獨立證據。兩支路都失效才失去功能的架構可降低獨立故障貢獻，卻不能消除共同原因。","textEn":"Examine whether two sensing channels share installation movement or electromagnetic exposure, avoiding treatment of correlated inputs as independent evidence. A function lost only when both branches fail can reduce independent contributions but cannot eliminate common causes.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「計軸感測共同原因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Common causes in axle sensing\" is correct?","options":["裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","本單元檢查兩個感測通道是否受同一安裝位移或電磁環境影響，避免把相關輸入當獨立證據。"],"optionsEn":["Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Examine whether two sensing channels share installation movement or electromagnetic exposure, avoiding treatment of correlated inputs as independent evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元檢查兩個感測通道是否受同一安裝位移或電磁環境影響，避免把相關輸入當獨立證據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Examine whether two sensing channels share installation movement or electromagnetic exposure, avoiding treatment of correlated inputs as independent evidence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b374-v16-30","title":"計軸感測共同原因：定量估算","titleEn":"Common causes in axle sensing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「計軸感測共同原因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Common causes in axle sensing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「計軸感測共同原因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Common causes in axle sensing\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車","取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty.","Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b374-v16-31","title":"計軸感測共同原因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Common causes in axle sensing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「計軸感測共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Common causes in axle sensing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「計軸感測共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in axle sensing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「計軸感測共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in axle sensing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「計軸感測共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in axle sensing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「計軸感測共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in axle sensing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「計軸感測共同原因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Common causes in axle sensing\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b374-v16-32","title":"計軸感測共同原因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Common causes in axle sensing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「計軸感測共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Common causes in axle sensing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「計軸感測共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in axle sensing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「計軸感測共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in axle sensing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「計軸感測共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Common causes in axle sensing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b374-v16-s5","title":"回滾與拆編情境與漏計試驗統計界限","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios & Statistical bounds for missed counts","description":"本階段聚焦「回滾與拆編情境」與「漏計試驗統計界限」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rollback and consist-change scenarios\" and \"Statistical bounds for missed counts\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b374-v16-33","title":"回滾與拆編情境：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「回滾與拆編情境」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rollback and consist-change scenarios” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元用離線事件序列覆蓋停住、反向與車組改變，逐項核對需求而不提供營運重置程序。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回滾與拆編情境」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use offline event sequences for stopping, reversal and consist changes, checking requirements without providing an operational reset procedure. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rollback and consist-change scenarios” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回滾與拆編情境」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rollback and consist-change scenarios”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-33-k1","title":"回滾與拆編情境","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios","text":"本單元用離線事件序列覆蓋停住、反向與車組改變，逐項核對需求而不提供營運重置程序。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。","textEn":"Use offline event sequences for stopping, reversal and consist changes, checking requirements without providing an operational reset procedure. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回滾與拆編情境」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rollback and consist-change scenarios\" is correct?","options":["本單元用離線事件序列覆蓋停住、反向與車組改變，逐項核對需求而不提供營運重置程序。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Use offline event sequences for stopping, reversal and consist changes, checking requirements without providing an operational reset procedure.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元用離線事件序列覆蓋停住、反向與車組改變，逐項核對需求而不提供營運重置程序。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use offline event sequences for stopping, reversal and consist changes, checking requirements without providing an operational reset procedure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b374-v16-34","title":"回滾與拆編情境：定量估算","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回滾與拆編情境」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rollback and consist-change scenarios” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回滾與拆編情境」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rollback and consist-change scenarios\", which statement holds?","options":["感測點越近就能在所有速度下得到越精準的速度","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Closer sensors always give more accurate speed at every operating speed.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b374-v16-35","title":"回滾與拆編情境：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回滾與拆編情境」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rollback and consist-change scenarios” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「回滾與拆編情境」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For rollback and consist-change scenarios, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「回滾與拆編情境」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for rollback and consist-change scenarios, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「回滾與拆編情境」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For rollback and consist-change scenarios, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「回滾與拆編情境」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for rollback and consist-change scenarios, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回滾與拆編情境」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rollback and consist-change scenarios\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只知道平均丟包率就能完全判定通訊可靠性","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The mean packet-loss rate completely determines communication reliability.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b374-v16-36","title":"回滾與拆編情境：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rollback and consist-change scenarios: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回滾與拆編情境」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rollback and consist-change scenarios” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「回滾與拆編情境」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for rollback and consist-change scenarios. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「回滾與拆編情境」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for rollback and consist-change scenarios. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回滾與拆編情境」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rollback and consist-change scenarios\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b374-v16-37","title":"漏計試驗統計界限：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Statistical bounds for missed counts: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「漏計試驗統計界限」如何影響計軸器列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Statistical bounds for missed counts” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Axle-counter train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將輪對測試紀錄按速度與輪型分層，說明單一條件下零漏計不能證明所有條件無誤。零次觀察到失效不代表真實失效機率為零。獨立伯努利試驗可由全數成功的機率反推單側上界，試驗數增加才會縮小界限；相關測試或只選容易案例會使這個統計推論不再成立，也不能由此宣告達到安全完整性等級。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏計試驗統計界限」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stratify wheelset trials by speed and wheel type, explaining why zero missed counts in one condition cannot establish error-free behaviour everywhere. Zero observed failures does not imply zero true failure probability. Independent Bernoulli trials allow a one-sided upper bound from the probability of all successes, which decreases with sample count. Correlated or selectively easy cases invalidate this inference and cannot establish a safety-integrity level. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Statistical bounds for missed counts” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漏計試驗統計界限」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Statistical bounds for missed counts”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-37-k1","title":"漏計試驗統計界限","titleEn":"Statistical bounds for missed counts","text":"本單元將輪對測試紀錄按速度與輪型分層，說明單一條件下零漏計不能證明所有條件無誤。零次觀察到失效不代表真實失效機率為零。","textEn":"Stratify wheelset trials by speed and wheel type, explaining why zero missed counts in one condition cannot establish error-free behaviour everywhere. Zero observed failures does not imply zero true failure probability.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏計試驗統計界限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Statistical bounds for missed counts\" is correct?","options":["完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","本單元將輪對測試紀錄按速度與輪型分層，說明單一條件下零漏計不能證明所有條件無誤。","進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車"],"optionsEn":["Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","Stratify wheelset trials by speed and wheel type, explaining why zero missed counts in one condition cannot establish error-free behaviour everywhere.","Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元將輪對測試紀錄按速度與輪型分層，說明單一條件下零漏計不能證明所有條件無誤。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stratify wheelset trials by speed and wheel type, explaining why zero missed counts in one condition cannot establish error-free behaviour everywhere. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b374-v16-38","title":"漏計試驗統計界限：定量估算","titleEn":"Statistical bounds for missed counts: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漏計試驗統計界限」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Statistical bounds for missed counts” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。公式 y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests)，代入得 y=0.00993608 failure probability。邊界：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Formula y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests) gives y=0.00993608 failure probability. Boundary: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。公式 y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests)，代入得 y=0.00993608 failure probability。邊界：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Formula y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests) gives y=0.00993608 failure probability. Boundary: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漏計試驗統計界限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Statistical bounds for missed counts\", which statement holds?","options":["取樣頻率固定時不同速度的空間解析度也一定相同","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。"],"optionsEn":["Fixed sampling frequency gives identical spatial resolution at every speed.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b374-v16-39","title":"漏計試驗統計界限：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Statistical bounds for missed counts: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漏計試驗統計界限」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Statistical bounds for missed counts” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。以「漏計試驗統計界限」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. For statistical bounds for missed counts, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把獨立試驗次數 tests 從 300 改成 301 independent trials（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.00993608 變為 0.00990324 failure probability。先說明「漏計試驗統計界限」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only independent trial count tests from 300 to 301 independent trials (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.00993608 to 0.00990324 failure probability. Explain the causal direction for statistical bounds for missed counts, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。以「漏計試驗統計界限」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. For statistical bounds for missed counts, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把獨立試驗次數 tests 從 300 改成 301 independent trials（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.00993608 變為 0.00990324 failure probability。先說明「漏計試驗統計界限」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only independent trial count tests from 300 to 301 independent trials (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.00993608 to 0.00990324 failure probability. Explain the causal direction for statistical bounds for missed counts, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漏計試驗統計界限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Statistical bounds for missed counts\"?","options":["核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b374-v16-40","title":"漏計試驗統計界限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Statistical bounds for missed counts: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"prerequisiteIds":["b374-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漏計試驗統計界限」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Statistical bounds for missed counts” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。回到「漏計試驗統計界限」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Trace the input chain for statistical bounds for missed counts. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b374-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。回到「漏計試驗統計界限」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Trace the input chain for statistical bounds for missed counts. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]},{"id":"b374-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏計試驗統計界限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Statistical bounds for missed counts\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。","進出計數剛好相同就能無條件證明區段無車"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption.","Equal entry and exit counts unconditionally prove that a section is empty."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-frauscher-2012"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b374-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b374-en.svg"}};
